{
  "requirement": "Give `outgoing_edges` a known source path and a label of the application’s\nedge-label type. Each path in `targets` can be used in a subsequent graph tool call.\n\n```text\noutgoing_edges({path: NodePath, label: EdgeLabel}) -> {targets: NodePath[]}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has three obligations. The tool takes a known source path and a label of the application's edge-label type. It returns `{targets: NodePath[]}`. Each returned path works in a later graph tool call.\n\n- **Result shape and reuse of targets.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[application_tools_preserve_graph_tools_in_the_same_conversation]` makes a real `outgoing_edges` call through the tool agent with path `1` and a label. It asserts that the tool result is not an error. It asserts that the result parses to exactly `{\"targets\":[{\"segments\":[\"2\"]}]}`. In the next turn the script calls `read_node` with that returned path `[\"2\"]`. The test asserts that the read succeeds with the expected 8192-character page. It also asserts that the dependencies recorded are `OutgoingEdges(Node(1), Label, ..)` followed by `Node(2)`. This covers \"each path in targets can be used in a subsequent graph tool call\".\n- **Tool exposure.** The same test asserts that every request lists `outgoing_edges` alongside the other graph tools.\n- **Label type.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[nested_label_schema_references_resolve_from_the_tool_parameters_root]` tests the tool's input schema from `edge_parameters::<Label>`. For a nested struct label, the `$ref` resolves from the parameters root. `path` and `label` are both required, and the label has no stray `$defs`. For a unit label, the `label` property has type `null`. This checks that the tool advertises the application's own edge-label type.\n- **Known source path.** The requirement only states a precondition for the path. `fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]` also exercises unknown paths and non-unit labels. It is marked for the behavior and inputs requirements, so I did not count it as evidence for this one. It does not leave a gap here.\n\nI read `GraphSession::tools` and `GraphSession::dispatch` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tools.rs` only to locate the implementation. I derived the expected behavior from the requirement text. I found no plausible violation that these assertions would accept.",
